Conversation Context Algorithm (FR-08):
function buildContext(conversationId, currentMessage):
    recent = fetchLastNMessages(conversationId, N=10)
    tokenBudget = MODEL_CONTEXT_LIMIT - SYSTEM_PROMPT_TOKENS
                 - estimateTokens(currentMessage) - RESPONSE_RESERVE (1000)
    contextMessages = []
    for msg in reverse(recent):
        msgTokens = estimateTokens(msg.content)
        if tokenBudget - msgTokens < 0: break
        contextMessages.prepend(msg)
        tokenBudget -= msgTokens
    return [SYSTEM_PROMPT, ...contextMessages, {role:'user', content: currentMessage}]

This implements an adaptive sliding window that prefers more recent context while never exceeding the model’s context limit — a safer approach than a hard-coded message count.
5.1.3 History Module
Aspect
