6.3 Physical Storage Considerations
Storage Engine: InnoDB — required for transactions, row-level locking, and foreign-key enforcement.
Character Set: utf8mb4 to support emoji and the full Unicode plane in message content.
Partitioning Strategy: For v1.0, no partitioning. When messages exceeds 10M rows (NFR-10), introduce monthly range partitioning on created_at:
ALTER TABLE messages
PARTITION BY RANGE (TO_DAYS(created_at)) (
  PARTITION p2025_01 VALUES LESS THAN (TO_DAYS('2025-02-01')),
  PARTITION p2025_02 VALUES LESS THAN (TO_DAYS('2025-03-01')),
  -- ...
  PARTITION pmax VALUES LESS THAN MAXVALUE
);

Read Replica: A read-only replica handles history browsing and admin dashboards; writes go to the primary.
