9.3 Database Optimization
Index strategy (already in §6.2 DDL):
users(email) UNIQUE — login lookup
conversations(user_id, updated_at DESC) — history list, FR-14
messages(conversation_id, created_at) — transcript load, FR-15
FULLTEXT messages(content) — search, FR-16
email_tokens(token_hash) UNIQUE — verification lookup
Query Budget: Every endpoint must complete its DB work in ≤100 ms p95 (leaving headroom under the NFR-10 500 ms ceiling). Slow queries (>200 ms) are auto-logged and triaged.
Connection Pooling: mysql2 pool with min=2, max=20 connections per Node instance. Pool exhaustion triggers a structured warning before reaching saturation.
9.4 Horizontal vs Vertical Scaling
Stateless app tier → horizontal: behind ALB, scale by container count (target: CPU 60% / memory 70%).
Database → vertical first, then read replicas: upgrade RDS instance class until ~70% CPU sustained, then add read replicas for history/admin read load.
Redis → vertical (single-instance with persistence) until v2.0, when Redis Cluster considered.
9.5 Load Balancing & CDN
L7 Load Balancer (AWS ALB or NGINX) with least-outstanding-requests algorithm — superior to round-robin for streaming workloads where some connections hold open longer.
SSE Connection Limits: ALB idle timeout raised to 120 s (max OpenAI streaming response). Browser limit of 6 SSE connections per origin documented; system uses a single multiplexed SSE per active chat.
CDN: Cloudflare for global edge caching of /assets/*, with brotli compression enabled.

10. ERROR HANDLING & LOGGING
10.1 Exception Handling Strategy
A three-tier error taxonomy:
// Tier 1: Domain errors (expected; map to 4xx)
class ValidationError extends DomainError { status = 400; }
class AuthenticationError extends DomainError { status = 401; }
class AuthorizationError extends DomainError { status = 403; }
class NotFoundError extends DomainError { status = 404; }
class RateLimitError extends DomainError { status = 429; }

// Tier 2: Integration errors (external; may retry; map to 502/503)
class UpstreamUnavailableError extends IntegrationError { status = 503; }
class UpstreamTimeoutError extends IntegrationError { status = 504; }

// Tier 3: Programmer errors (bugs; map to 500 + alert)
class UnexpectedError extends Error { status = 500; }

A central Express error-handling middleware:
Logs the error with full context.
Sanitizes the response (no stack traces in production).
Returns the standard RFC-7807 envelope.
Unhandled rejection / uncaught exception: Logged, then the process exits and is restarted by the container orchestrator — preventing zombie state.
10.2 Logging Framework & Levels
Library: Pino (fastest JSON logger; ~5× Winston).
Format: Structured JSON, one event per line.
Correlation: Every request gets requestId (UUID) injected via middleware; propagated to all logs and to downstream OpenAI calls as X-Request-ID.
PII Hygiene (NFR-05): A custom redactor strips password, token, authorization, content (message body) fields before serialization.
