14. APPENDICES
Appendix A — Glossary
Context Window — The set of recent messages sent to the LLM along with a new user query, enabling continuity.
Hallucination — Plausible-sounding but factually incorrect output from an LLM.
Prompt Injection — An attack where user input manipulates the model into ignoring its system prompt.
SSE (Server-Sent Events) — A one-way HTTP-based streaming protocol used to push tokens from server to browser.
System Prompt — A hidden instruction prepended to every LLM call to constrain behavior (e.g., “You are a helpful academic assistant…”).
Token — The atomic unit of LLM input/output (~¾ of a word in English).
PITR (Point-In-Time Recovery) — Restoring a database to any moment within the retention window using binary logs.
